{"advance_requested_at_utc":"2026-10-11T14:46:10.796906+00:00","confirmed_proved":true,"job_id":"e7377b25-c4cc-4efb-a58f-3fda319e5ef1","last_publish_verdict":{"body":{"created_at":"2026-10-11T14:46:14.321584+00:00","definitions":"import Mathlib.Tactic\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_InterpolationMatrix_CoreData\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_RowTranslation_CoreData\nimport Theorems.Thm_OAI_PiExponent_Arithmetic_shifted_truncation_product_coeff_gaussian\n\nopen OAI.PiExponent OAI.PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix\nopen scoped BigOperators\n\n","error_message":"","formal_statement":"theorem OAI.PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix.entry_truncatedLog_cleared_gaussian {m : ℕ}\r\n    (T q e : Fin m → ℕ) (p : Fin m → ℤ) (hq : ∀ i, q i ≠ 0)\r\n    (j s h : ℕ) (β α : Fin m → ℕ) (hα : ∀ i, α i ≤ e i) :\r\n    (∏ i, (Nat.lcmUpto (T i) : ℂ) ^ e i) *\r\n      (∏ i, (q i : ℂ) ^ α i) / (∏ i, (q i : ℂ) ^ β i) *\r\n      entry (fun i => 2 * Complex.I * (p i : ℂ) / (q i : ℂ))\r\n        (fun i => truncatedLog (T i)) j s β h α ∈ GaussianInt.toComplex.range := by\n  sorry\n","id":"e7377b25-c4cc-4efb-a58f-3fda319e5ef1","kind":"problem","natural_language_statement":"Fix $m$ coordinates and natural vectors $T,q,e$, integer numerators $p$, and assume $q_i\\ne0$. Let $j,s,h$ be natural numbers and let $\\alpha,\\beta\\in\\mathbb N^m$ satisfy $\\alpha_i\\le e_i$. Set $r_i=2\\mathrm i p_i/q_i$, $G_i=\\ell_{T_i}(X)$, and $L_i=\\operatorname{lcm}(1,\\ldots,T_i)$, where $\\ell_T$ is the polynomial truncation of $\\log(1+X)$. The original interpolation entry $A_{j,s,\\beta;h,\\alpha}$ then satisfies\n\n$$\\left(\\prod_iL_i^{e_i}\\right)\\frac{\\prod_iq_i^{\\alpha_i}}{\\prod_iq_i^{\\beta_i}}A_{j,s,\\beta;h,\\alpha}\\in\\mathbb Z[\\mathrm i]\\subset\\mathbb C.$$\n\nThis clears the denominators of the logarithmic interpolation matrix at Gaussian rational centers.","source":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Approximation/MatrixArithmetic.lean#L74-L126","status":"PUBLISHED","tags":["number-theory","polynomial","linear-algebra","openai-pi-exponent-017"],"theorem_id":"922f6b18-bfda-41a8-9f45-ff48f8cec8a4","theorem_name":"OAI.PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix.entry_truncatedLog_cleared_gaussian","theorem_title":"Gaussian integrality of cleared truncated-logarithm interpolation entries","updated_at":"2026-10-11T14:47:30.587576+00:00","visibility":"public"},"http_status":200},"last_verify_verdict":{"body":{"created_at":"2026-10-11T14:48:31.658219+00:00","error_message":"","file_path":"922f6b18-bfda-41a8-9f45-ff48f8cec8a4/418b0711-62a5-416a-ba5d-876ae8758fe3/643ea42c-eb36-4a8b-9440-b65e0ab348b3.lean","id":"643ea42c-eb36-4a8b-9440-b65e0ab348b3","status":"ACCEPTED","theorem_id":"922f6b18-bfda-41a8-9f45-ff48f8cec8a4","updated_at":"2026-10-11T14:51:50.821332+00:00","user_id":"418b0711-62a5-416a-ba5d-876ae8758fe3"},"http_status":200},"preparation":{"API_used":false,"actual_provider_bindings":{"closed_AP13_child":{"certificate":"verification/ap14/shifted-child-mirror/local-child-validation.json","certificate_sha256":"3b6ca8da6eb6fa6631561552e774a2895544ea0a60c82c267adbdbc6967c59c4","module":"Theorems.Thm_OAI_PiExponent_Arithmetic_shifted_truncation_product_coeff_gaussian","olean":"verification/staged-build/lib/lean/Theorems/Thm_OAI_PiExponent_Arithmetic_shifted_truncation_product_coeff_gaussian.olean","olean_sha256":"5c1084a5cd7abb68716a701307578e136ed512a713c516d120da737e81a590fb"},"interpolation":{"certificate":"verification/ap10/interpolation/actual-provider-validation.json","certificate_sha256":"1eb1e28af81f2a63a11ba6006a1b3dea8f2c08aa8841643b831a3e4ea7924526","module":"Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_InterpolationMatrix_CoreData","olean":"verification/staged-build/lib/lean/Definitions/Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_InterpolationMatrix_CoreData.olean","olean_sha256":"53cb7c979589f09b3db49a266b652d