^{\\beta_i}}A_{j,s,\\beta;h,\\alpha}\\in\\mathbb Z[\\mathrm i]\\subset\\mathbb C.$$\n\nThis clears the denominators of the logarithmic interpolation matrix at Gaussian rational centers.","preamble":"import Mathlib.Tactic\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_InterpolationMatrix_CoreData\nimport Definitions.Def_OAI_NumberTheory_PiExponent_Approximation_RowTranslation_CoreData\nimport Theorems.Thm_OAI_PiExponent_Arithmetic_shifted_truncation_product_coeff_gaussian\n\nopen OAI.PiExponent OAI.PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix\nopen scoped BigOperators\n\n","readback":null,"source":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Approximation/MatrixArithmetic.lean#L74-L126","status":"Proved","tags":["linear-algebra","number-theory","openai-pi-exponent-017","polynomial"],"theorem_id":"922f6b18-bfda-41a8-9f45-ff48f8cec8a4","theorem_name":"OAI.PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix.entry_truncatedLog_cleared_gaussian","theorem_title":"Gaussian integrality of cleared truncated-logarithm interpolation entries","visibility":"public","vote_count":0},"http_status":200},"theorem_id":"922f6b18-bfda-41a8-9f45-ff48f8cec8a4","theorem_name":"OAI.PiExponent.InterpolationMatrix.entry_truncatedLog_cleared_gaussian","updated_at_utc":"2026-10-11T14:52:36.739391+00:00","verify_intent":{"at_utc":"2026-10-11T14:48:30.381539+00:00","content_type":"multipart/form-data; boundary=----p2mBoundary7f3a9c2b","descriptor_sha256":"94494c34897766d43b6746858ce535221356bf4f3c21236d2234a8c444c62c94","multipart_sha256":"2110d746cddf7d9ded7138ea7ed7588d58daefc873d5b007a7bea9481aa99e23","solution_sha256":"c3eebdb377bbfd554755c49560e5542d4c5d297f36bcd18f5ce5b3d61c1b85ca","theorem_id":"922f6b18-bfda-41a8-9f45-ff48f8cec8a4"},"verify_response":{"body":{"guidelines":"Reminder: write the explanation like a section of a math paper, not a tactic-by-tactic transcript. Walk through the mathematical argument and show how it maps onto your Le